# What this reaches for (format `<path> <name>`, path relative to this dir):
# the Go script worker, which supplies the interpreter and the container.
# std/deep-deps mounts it at DEEP-DEPS/go, which `.caos-expr` names as --base.
#
# ITS OWN DEPS COME WITH IT. std/go is evaluable (`run
# --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake-builder --in:@=. --lock:@=DEEP-DEPS/flake.lock`), so
# it needs a flake-builder and a lock of its own — and deepening is RECURSIVE,
# filling DEEP-DEPS/go/DEEP-DEPS/{flake-builder,flake.lock} from std/go's DEPS
# without this file naming either. Measured in the deepened tree.
#
# So a consumer declares only what its OWN expression names. Declaring a
# mount's dependencies as well is redundant, which is what 26 test DEPS files
# were doing with flake-builder.
../../../std/go go
